00:43:40.000 --> 00:44:52.000
The young man kept his head bowed throughout most of the service, until he was summoned before the crowd to deliver his eulogy. Seth lamented his father as his hero, referencing his childhood terror of being trapped after the Lausanne earthquake, before Teddy bravely rescued him. He expressed sadness at now never knowing the backstory of his unique name. A story Teddy had promised to reveal on Seth's 21st birthday. Seth said, I will never find out the meaning of my name because it was taken away along with my father. That part of me will always be incomplete. At the conclusion of Seth's eulogy, he took a deep breath, and in an act that would be later described by witnesses as bizarre and uncomfortable, he began singing a solo acapella rendition of the R&B ballad One Sweet Day by Mariah Carey and Boys to Men. It was a flawless performance given without a single tear, regarded by listeners as emotionally detached, self-indulgent, and inappropriate given the somber circumstances of the gathering.
这个年轻人几乎在整个仪式中都低着头，直到他被召集到人群前发表悼词。塞思将父亲哀悼为他的英雄，他回忆起自己童年时在洛桑地震后被困的恐惧，当时泰迪勇敢地救了他。他为现在永远无法得知自己独特名字的背景而感到悲伤。泰迪曾承诺在塞思21岁生日时揭晓这个故事。塞思说：“我永远不会知道我名字的含义，因为它随着我的父亲一起被剥夺了。我生命中的那部分将永远不完整。”在塞思的悼词结束时，他深吸了一口气，做出了一个后来被目击者描述为诡异且令人不适的举动——他开始独唱玛丽亚·凯莉和大人小孩双人组的R&B抒情歌曲《甜蜜的一天》（One Sweet Day）。这是一场完美无瑕的表演，没有流下一滴眼泪，在听众看来，鉴于聚会阴郁的环境，这种表现显得情感抽离、自我放纵且不合时宜。

37
00:44:52.000 --> 00:45:49.000
Teddy, Loiva and Claudine were buried together on the grounds of Macquarie Park Cemetery. Their memorial plaques declaring their cherished trio would forever live in the hearts and smiles of those they left behind, including Seth. It hadn't just been funeral attendees who had noticed Seth Gonzalez's odd behaviour in the days following the murder of his family. Police were suspicious of Seth from the moment he made the frantic call to triple zero on the late night of July 10, 2001. Sorry? What? Someone's what? What trouble are you in?
泰迪、洛伊弗和克劳丁被合葬在麦考瑞公园公墓的土地上。他们的纪念牌匾上刻着，他们深爱的三人组将永远活在包括塞思在内的那些他们留下的人的心中和微笑里。不仅仅是葬礼出席者注意到了塞思·冈萨雷斯在家人被谋杀后的几天里的古怪行为。从2001年7月10日深夜塞思拨打紧急求救电话的那一刻起，警方就对塞思产生了怀疑。抱歉？什么？谁的什么？你遇到了什么麻烦？

38
00:45:49.000 --> 00:46:50.000
What trouble are you in? North ride. And your parents are by saying shot, have they? No. Yeah, we will. We will send in ambulance now. Minutes after midnight on July 11, 2001, first responders raced to Collins Street following alarming reports that a gunman was active in the area. They arrived to the scene, a nondescript homestead belonging to the Filipino-Australian Gonzalez family, where they found a 20-year-old Seth Gonzalez sitting on the floor of the open garage. The young man was in hysterics, imploring paramedics and police officers to enter his house and help his family.
你遇到了什么麻烦？北赖德。你的父母说他们被枪击了吗？没有。是的，我们会。我们现在就派救护车去。2001年7月11日午夜过后几分钟，急救人员冲向柯林斯街，此前有惊人的报告称该地区有枪手活动。他们到达了现场，这是一处属于菲澳裔冈萨雷斯一家的普通住宅，他们在敞开的车库地板上找到了20岁的塞思·冈萨雷斯。这个年轻人歇斯底里，恳求医护人员和警察进入他的家并帮助他的家人。

39
00:46:50.000 --> 00:47:54.000
Attending police were quick to notice Seth Gonzalez's odd behaviour at the scene. Although sobbing intensely, Seth's face remained completely dry, not a single tear was shed. He appeared frenzied and panicked, yet his answers to questions were noticeably thought out and rational. He claimed to have performed CPR on both of his parents and later added he had tended to the wounds of his sister with his bare hands. There was bloodstaining on the leg of his jeans, a little on the back sleeve of his jumper, as well as a few spots on his boots. Barely anything given the state of the victims. Seth was quick to offer a dubious explanation, claiming that the rain, at which point was only a drizzle, had washed most of the bloodstaining from his clothing and he had wiped the remainder from his hands onto the damp lawn. An astute police officer noticed some blue coloured staining on the left sleeve of Seth's jumper towards the edge of the cuff.
出警的警察很快注意到塞思·冈萨雷斯在现场的古怪行为。尽管痛苦地啜泣，但塞思的脸完全是干的，没有流下一滴眼泪。他显得狂乱和惊慌，但对问题的回答却明显经过深思熟虑且合乎理性。他声称对他的父母都实施了心肺复苏术，后来又补充说他曾用双手处理了妹妹的伤口。他的牛仔裤腿上有血迹，套头衫的后袖上有一点，靴子上也有几个点。考虑到受害者的状况，这几乎不算什么。塞思很快给出了一个可疑的解释，声称当时只是细雨，雨水已经冲刷掉了他衣服上的大部分血迹，他把剩下的血迹从手上擦到了潮湿的草坪上。一名精明的警察注意到塞思套头衫的左袖口边缘有一些蓝色的污渍。

40
00:47:54.000 --> 00:49:17.000
The colour resembled the spray paint used to graffiti racial obscenities on an interior wall in the Gonzalez house. Later analysis determined this staining on Seth's jumper was indeed a blue paint. A shoebox was found in a wardrobe in Seth's bedroom and according to the label had had originally contained a pair of UK size 7 human brand running shoes. The shoes themselves were missing from Seth's footwear collection, but were an exact match to the bloody footprints tracked through the crime scene by the killer. Seth insisted the shoes had never belonged to him, they had been purchased by his father for a cousin who lived in the Philippines. Knowing a thorough search of his bedroom was underway, Seth confided to a police officer about a pornographic video he had hidden away in a dresser drawer and he appeared very embarrassed by the prospect of investigators finding it. Given the tragic circumstances, the officer felt uncomfortable that Seth's primary concern was about his pornography stash and not the murder of his family. Nearly a week after the murders, Seth Gonzalez was escorted by police to Collins Street after agreeing to participate in a full reenactment of the night of July 10.
这种颜色类似于冈萨雷斯家内墙上喷涂种族主义粗言秽语的喷漆。后来的分析确定，塞思套头衫上的这种污渍确实是蓝色油漆。在塞思卧室的衣柜里发现了一个鞋盒，根据标签，它原本装着一双英国7码的人类品牌跑步鞋。鞋子本身从塞思的鞋柜里不见了，但与凶手在犯罪现场留下的血脚印完全吻合。塞思坚信这双鞋从来不属于他，它们是他父亲为住在菲律宾的一个表亲买的。得知对他的卧室的彻底搜查正在进行中，塞思向一名警察吐露了他藏在梳妆台抽屉里的色情录影带，并且对调查人员发现它的可能性显得非常尴尬。鉴于悲惨的环境，这名警官感到不安的是，塞思最关心的居然是他藏匿的色情制品，而不是他家人的谋杀案。谋杀案发生近一周后，塞思·冈萨雷斯在同意参与7月10日晚上的完整情景重现后，被警方护送到柯林斯街。

41
00:49:17.000 --> 00:50:53.000
Calmly and precisely, Seth retraced and described his movements upon finding the brutalized bodies of his parents and sister. At no time did he indicate reliving these traumatic events was causing him any distress. Of particular interest to investigators was the claims Seth had witnessed the perpetrator fleeing the house and had subsequently given chase. Police tested this theory and determined by the time Seth would have exited the house via the garage and emerged under Collins Street, the killer would have most certainly been long gone and completely out of sight. CCTV footage retrieved from cameras within Sydney's CBD confirmed Seth's alibi on the night of July 10, proving he had dined out and played arcade games with a friend between the hours of 8pm and 11pm. Seth's claims that he was out driving around Kings Grove prior to this meetup could not be verified, nor could his whereabouts between the crucial time frame in which the murders were carried out, sometime between 4pm and 7pm. A client of Teddy Gonzalez's law firm Tile Police, they had stopped by the Collins Street home between 4.10pm and 4.30pm on July 10, around the approximate time Claudine was killed. As this witness dropped some documents into the Gonzalez's letterbox, they recalled seeing a green Ford Festiva parked out the front of the house.
塞思冷静而精确地回溯并描述了他发现父母和妹妹遭受残酷虐待的尸体时的举动。他没有表现出任何因重温这些创伤性事件而感到痛苦的迹象。调查人员特别感兴趣的是，塞思声称自己目睹了凶手逃离房屋并随后进行了追捕。警方对这一理论进行了测试，并确定当塞思通过车库离开房屋并出现在柯林斯街时，凶手肯定已经走得很远，完全消失在视线之外了。悉尼中央商务区内摄像头调取的闭路电视画面证实了塞思在7月10日晚上的不在场证明，证明他在晚上8点到11点之间与朋友一起外出用餐并玩了街机游戏。塞思声称在此次聚会之前他开车在金斯格罗夫附近兜风的说法无法得到证实，他在实施谋杀的关键时间段（即下午4点到晚上7点之间）的行踪也无法证实。泰迪·冈萨雷斯律师事务所的一位客户向警方反映，他们在7月10日下午4点10分到4点30分之间曾在柯林斯街的家中停留，大约是在克劳丁被杀害的时间前后。当这名目击者将一些文件投入冈萨雷斯的信箱时，他们回忆说看到一辆绿色的福特福斯蒂瓦停在房子前面。

42
00:50:53.000 --> 00:52:11.000
This was not the only witness who saw Seth Gonzalez's vehicle parked at the Collins Street address within the time frame of the murders. Emily Luna, Seth's aunt, had visited the Gonzalez home at approximately 6pm on July 10 and recalled Seth's Ford Festiva was parked in the carport. She believed someone was home at the time as she had spotted movement through a window and noted the kitchen light was on, yet when Emily rang the doorbell several times, there was no answer. Emily's statement wasn't surprising given that Seth's written statement also declared he had stopped by the house around this time. Seth said it had been raining so he remained in the car and had never entered the house before deciding to drive off to Kingsgrove to visit his friend. Yet, Emily Luna provided two crucial details during her interviews that contradicted Seth's statement. Firstly, Emily distinctly remembered it was not raining when she visited the house as she didn't require the use of her umbrella. During further talks with police, Emily also admitted that she did not see Seth sitting in his vehicle at the time.
这不是唯一一个在谋杀案发生时间段内看到塞思·冈萨雷斯的车停在柯林斯街地址的目击者。塞思的姑姑艾米丽·卢娜在7月10日晚上6点左右拜访了冈萨雷斯家，并回忆说塞思的福特福斯蒂瓦停在车棚里。她相信当时家里有人，因为她透过窗户看到有动静，并注意到厨房的灯亮着，然而当艾米丽按了几次门铃时，却无人应答。艾米丽的证词并不令人意外，因为塞思的书面供词也声明他大约在这个时间在房子外面停过。塞思说当时在下雨，所以他留在车里，在决定开车去金斯格罗夫拜访朋友之前，从来没有进过房子。然而，艾米丽·卢娜在接受采访时提供了两个关键细节，与塞思的供词相矛盾。首先，艾米丽清楚地记得她拜访房子时并没有下雨，因为她不需要使用雨伞。在与警方进一步交谈时，艾米丽还承认，她当时并没有看到塞思坐在车里。

43
00:52:11.000 --> 00:53:39.000
The two suspected murder weapons, a knife believed to have been sourced from the Gonzalez kitchen and a baseball bat, had not been recovered. According to Seth's close friend Sam, Seth mentioned he kept a baseball bat in the boot of his car as a means of self-protection. When questioned about the bat, Seth said he may have carried one in the past, but he couldn't account for its current whereabouts. Investigators were certain Seth was being deceitful, but it wasn't until they began questioning his friends and extended social group that they uncovered the sheer extent of deception the 20-year-old had cultivated throughout the years. Seth gloated to acquaintances of being a Taekwondo expert who ran his own security company, owned property, and frequently traveled to New York to negotiate elaborate business deals. He also claimed to be the manager of a boy band, a music producer, a successful singer with a record deal, a world champion kickboxer, a lawyer, a personal trainer, and the manager of a modeling agency. In early 2000, Seth broke the news to friends that he had been diagnosed with cancer, later revealing he had beaten the disease and was now in remission. The depth of Seth's deception went far deeper than seemingly harmless arrogant brags to friends and associates.
两件疑似凶器——一把据信取自冈萨雷斯厨房的刀和一个棒球棍——尚未找到。根据塞思的好友萨姆所说，塞思曾提到他在汽车后备箱里放了一根棒球棍作为防身之用。当被问及这根棒球棍时，塞思说他过去可能带过一根，但他无法解释它现在的去向。调查人员确信塞思在说谎，但直到他们开始盘问他的朋友和扩大社交圈时，他们才发现这个20岁年轻人多年来编造的谎言规模有多大。塞思向熟人吹嘘自己是精通跆拳道并经营自己安保公司的专家、拥有房产，并经常前往纽约谈判复杂的商业交易。他还声称自己是一个男子乐队的经理、音乐制作人、拥有唱片合约的成功歌手、世界自由搏击冠军、律师、私人教练以及模特公司的经理。2000年初，塞思向朋友们爆料称自己被诊断出患有癌症，后来又透露他已经战胜了疾病并处于缓解期。塞思欺骗的深度远远超过了对朋友和同事看似无害的傲慢吹嘘。

44
00:53:39.000 --> 00:54:58.000
Music was clearly Seth's greatest passion, yet his R&B group, Definite Vibes, had two staunch critics, his own parents. Teddy and Oliver were vocal about their disapproval of their son's musical ambitions as it had caused everything else in his life to fall by the wayside, including his education. Seth failed to submit assignments or attend exams, his musical priorities having irreversible negative impact on his medical science degree, which he hastily dropped out of. His parents threatened to take away his beloved car if his studies didn't improve, which would strip the 20-year-old of his independence. Teddy and Oliver were pleased when Seth started achieving high results in his new legal studies degree, indicating a positive change in his attitude. However, it was discovered Seth had been falsifying university documents to deceive his parents into thinking he was doing much better than he was. In reality, Seth was failing all four of his subjects. The truth about Seth's academic failure and forgery had only recently been exposed to Teddy and Oliver, their disappointment causing a rift between son and parents.
音乐显然是塞思最大的热情，但他的R&B组合“确定氛围”（Definite Vibes）有两个坚定的批评者——他自己的父母。泰迪和洛伊弗直言不讳地表达了他们对儿子音乐雄心的不赞成，因为这导致了他生活中的其他一切都被荒废了，包括他的教育。塞思未能按时交作业或参加考试，他的音乐优先事项对他的医学科学学位产生了不可逆转的负面影响，他匆忙退学了。他的父母威胁说，如果他的学业没有改善，就要收回他心爱的汽车，这将剥夺这个20岁年轻人的独立性。当塞思在他的新法律学位课程中取得高成绩时，泰迪和洛伊弗很高兴，这表明他的态度有了积极的转变。然而，人们发现塞思一直在伪造大学文件，以欺骗他的父母，让他们以为他比实际情况做得好得多。实际上，塞思的四门科目全都不及格。关于塞思学业失败和伪造的真相最近才被揭露给泰迪和洛伊弗，他们的失望导致了儿子与父母之间的裂痕。

45
00:54:58.000 --> 00:56:02.000
Adding fuel to this tension was Seth's romantic relationships. He introduced one girlfriend to his mother in the hopes of gaining her approval, but loyver was dismissive, expressing concerns a girlfriend would only be another distraction to Seth's studies. Seth's parents threatened to disinherit him if he continued to see his girlfriend, leading the relationship to come to an end. Seth's temperamental relationship with his parents may have had roots in his upbringing. Although the Gonzales parents were loving, Seth was harshly disciplined when he misbehaved during his childhood. It appeared Seth carried the emotional baggage from his youth into his adult years, which manifested in frequent bedwetting. Loyver had encouraged Seth to seek professional help for this reoccurring issue, but her attempts to assist were futile. The true level of Seth's dishonesty was exposed when a family friend accused him of stealing money from her purse.
给这种紧张关系火上浇油的是塞思的恋爱关系。他把一个女朋友介绍给母亲，希望能得到母亲的批准，但洛伊弗却不屑一顾，表达了这样的担忧：女朋友只会分散塞思学业的精力。塞思的父母威胁说，如果他继续和这个女朋友交往，就要剥夺他的继承权，导致这段恋情走到了尽头。塞思与父母之间暴躁的关系可能植根于他的成长经历。虽然冈萨雷斯的父母很有爱心，但塞思在童年行为不端时受到了严厉的惩罚。塞思似乎把童年的情感包袱带到了成年期，这表现为频繁的夜尿症。洛伊弗曾鼓励塞思为这个反复出现的问题寻求专业帮助，但她试图提供的帮助是徒劳的。当一个家庭朋友指责塞思从她的钱包里偷钱时，塞思撒谎的真正程度暴露了。

46
00:56:02.000 --> 00:57:12.000
Seth didn't deny the allegation, simply saying he was an opportunist. It came as little surprise to Teddy or Loyver when they found out, as they had suspected for some time that Seth was stealing cash from their wallets. After his parents and sister were murdered, Seth was approved a $15,000 payment from the government as part of a victims of crime compensation scheme. However, he didn't use this money to pay for his family's funeral or his own living expenses as it was intended. Instead, he used part of the payout for cosmetic enhancements to his mother's car, which he had taken to driving following her murder. The overwhelming circumstantial evidence was mounting against Seth Gonzales, who stood to gain immense profit from the deaths of his parents. Especially if his sister was removed from the equation. Seth vehemently denied accusations of involvement in the crime, alleging that a hit had been taken out on his family by one of his father's wealthy, influential Filipino business rivals.
塞思没有否认这一指控，只是说他是个机会主义者。当泰迪或洛伊弗发现时，他们并没有感到太意外，因为他们一段时间以来一直怀疑塞思在偷他们钱包里的现金。父母和妹妹被谋杀后，塞思根据犯罪受害者赔偿计划获得了政府1.5万澳元的批准金。然而，他并没有像原本打算的那样用这笔钱来支付家人的葬礼或他自己的生活费用。相反，他将部分赔偿金用于对母亲的汽车进行外观升级，自从母亲被谋杀后，他便开始开这辆车。压倒性的间接证据正在对塞思·冈萨雷斯不利，他将从父母的死中获得巨大的利益。特别是如果他的妹妹也被排除在方程式之外的话。塞思强烈否认参与这起犯罪的指控，声称他的家人是被他父亲的一个富有、有影响力的菲律宾商业竞争对手买凶杀害的。

47
00:57:12.000 --> 00:58:28.000
Seth believed the killers intentionally spared one family member to serve as the scapegoat, and was living in fear that someone would be coming for him next. It wasn't a completely inconceivable prospect, as a colleague of Teddy's had overheard the immigration lawyer aggressively arguing and swearing on the phone with a Filipino property investor months prior to the murders. According to Teddy, the caller threatened to kill his family. But other than Teddy's word, investigators failed to find any concrete evidence to support this threat was ever made. They identified several business rivals of Teddy's who may have stood to gain marginally from his death. Yet, they lacked motive to order the deaths of Loewe and Claudine, and subsequent investigations ruled them out as suspects. Despite this, the hitman theory arose again in August, when Seth Gonzales handed police a copy of an anonymous email he had received a month after the murders. Written in a mix of English and Tagalog, the email stated a hitman was paid for three murders, and implied Seth had been the intended third target alongside his parents.
塞思认为凶手故意留下一名家庭成员作为替罪羊，并生活在恐惧之中，生怕有人会下一个找上他。这并非一个完全不可想象的前景，因为泰迪的一位同事曾听到这位移民律师在谋杀案发生前几个月，与一名菲律宾房地产投资者在电话里进行激烈的争吵和咒骂。据泰迪说，打电话的人威胁要杀死他的全家。但除了泰迪的一面之词外，调查人员未能找到任何具体证据来支持这一威胁曾经被发出过。他们确定了几位泰迪的商业竞争对手，这些人可能从他的死中获得微薄的利益。然而，他们缺乏下令杀害洛伊弗和克劳丁的动机，随后的调查排除了他们作为嫌疑人的可能。尽管如此，杀手理论在8月再次出现，当时塞思·冈萨雷斯向警方交出了一份他在谋杀案发生一个月后收到的一封匿名电子邮件的复印件。这封邮件由英文和他加禄语混写，称杀手为三起谋杀案获得了报酬，并暗示塞思是除了他父母之外的第三个预定目标。

48
00:58:28.000 --> 00:59:31.000
The email read, You're supposed to be the third person. They were paid for three. It's a blessing that you were not there. Seth was convinced his life was still in danger, enlisting friends to act as bodyguards. Police later seized Seth's personal computers and found a draft of the threatening email stored on one of them. Seth had written it himself. Seth's aunt, Emily Luna, refused to accept that her baby-faced nephew could be guilty for the violent triple murder, despite recognizing many inconsistencies in his statements and having some awareness that he was not the perfect son. Nevertheless, Emily remained supportive of Seth, even holding his hand as he gave his first interview with police regarding July 10. Emily listened as Seth detailed driving to the Gonzales house at 6pm before departing soon after.
邮件写道：“你应该是第三个人。他们付了三个人的钱。你不在那里真是一种保佑。”塞思确信自己的生命仍然处于危险之中，于是招募朋友充当保镖。警方后来查获了塞思的个人电脑，并在其中一台电脑上发现了一份威胁邮件的草稿。塞思是自己写的。塞思的姑姑艾米丽·卢娜拒绝接受她那娃娃脸的侄子会是这起暴力三起谋杀案的凶手，尽管她承认他的供词中有许多矛盾之处，并且意识到他并不是完美的儿子。尽管如此，艾米丽仍然支持塞思，甚至在他接受关于7月10日的第一次警方采访时握着他的手。艾米丽听着塞思详细描述他在下午6点开车去冈萨雷斯家，不久后便离开的经过。

49
00:59:31.000 --> 01:00:58.000
It was his remark that the rain prevented him from getting out of his car that caused Emily's hand to instinctively jerk away from Seth's. She stopped by the house at 6pm and knew without a doubt that it had not been raining, and Seth was not in his car. It was in that moment the haunting realization dawned on Emily. She knew her nephew was lying. Upon accepting the possibility that Seth may be responsible for the brutal murder of her sister, brother-in-law and niece, Emily agreed to discreetly work with investigators against her nephew. A listening device was installed in her car and a plan constructed in which she was to tell Seth she knew he was responsible for the killings and wanted to protect him. But the ploy didn't work. Not only did Seth continually deny having anything to do with the crime, he also told Emily he was so depressed over the matter that he was considering taking his own life. Two months after the murders of Teddy, Lover and Claudine Gonzales, Seth was at a coffee shop when a passer-by complimented him on his clothing. Flattered, Seth struck up a conversation with a man who revealed himself to be a gangster with connections to the police force.
正是他关于“雨水阻止了他下车”的言论，让艾米丽的手本能地从塞思的手中抽开。她在下午6点顺道去了那栋房子，并且百分之百确定当时根本没有下雨，塞思也根本不在他的车里。就在那一刻，令人挥之不去的 realization 黎明般在艾米丽脑海中浮现。她知道她的侄子在说谎。在接受了塞思可能对她的姐姐、姐夫和侄女的残酷谋杀负责的可能性后，艾米丽同意秘密与调查人员合作，对抗她的侄子。一个监听设备被安装在她的车里，并制定了一个计划：她要告诉塞思，她知道他是这些谋杀案的幕后黑手，并且想要保护他。但这个计策没有奏效。塞思不仅不断否认与这起犯罪有任何关系，他还告诉艾米丽，他对此事感到非常沮丧，以至于正在考虑结束自己的生命。泰迪、洛伊弗和克劳丁·冈萨雷斯被谋杀两个月后，塞思正在一家咖啡馆里，一个路人称赞了他的衣着。塞思深受奉承，便和一个自称是与警方有联系的黑帮分子的男子攀谈起来。

50
01:00:58.000 --> 01:02:00.000
Seth claimed he too was in a gang called the White Dragons Asian. In truth, there was no such gang. Seth made it up. The two build a rapport, forming a friendship over the following weeks. The man was aware of the allegations Seth was facing and in an act of good faith offered his new friend an opportunity. He knew a guy in prison who was dying and who was willing to take the rap for crimes he didn't commit. If Seth wanted to, the terminal prisoner could confess to the Gonzales family murders on Seth's behalf, taking the heat off him completely. In the end, Seth didn't accept the offer, only going so far as providing the gangster with hand-drawn floor plans at the Gonzales home, marked with the location where each member of his family was found. Unbeknownst to Seth, his gangster friend was actually an undercover police officer.
塞思声称自己也加入了一个名为“亚洲白龙”（White Dragons Asian）的帮派。事实上，根本没有这样的帮派。是塞思编造的。两人一拍即合，在接下来的几周里建立了友谊。这名男子知道塞思面临的指控，出于善意，他为新朋友提供了一个机会。他认识监狱里的一个人快死了，愿意为一个他没有犯下的罪行顶罪。如果塞思愿意，这个身患绝症的囚犯可以代表塞思承认冈萨雷斯一家的谋杀案，从而彻底消除他的压力。最后，塞思并没有接受这个提议，只是向黑帮分子提供了冈萨雷斯家手绘的平面图，上面标明了找到他家人中每个成员的位置。塞思不知道的是，他的黑帮朋友实际上是一名卧底警察。

51
01:02:00.000 --> 01:03:08.000
Police promptly compared Seth's handwriting from the map provided to the undercover officer so the racist graffiti on the internal wall of the Gonzales house and found slight similarities between the two. That wasn't the only valuable piece of information Seth had unwittingly provided. On the floor plan, he had also noted the time of death of each family member. Information police had intentionally withheld, as it was a detail only the killer would know. During the surveillance, Seth told the undercover officer, People don't suspect me. It's just Seth with the little baby face. I have a split personality. I can hide what I do. They've got nothing on me. It's all circumstantial stuff. However, as the undercover operation progressed, Seth didn't confess, telling the undercover officer he was not involved in the murders and maintaining his story that a contract killer hired by one of his father's rivals was responsible for the crime.
警方迅速将地图上塞思的笔迹与冈萨雷斯家内墙上的种族主义涂鸦进行对比，发现两者有微小的相似之处。这并不是塞思无意中提供的唯一有价值的信息。在平面图上，他还标注了每个家庭成员的死亡时间。这是警方故意隐瞒的信息，因为这是只有凶手才知道的细节。在监视期间，塞思告诉卧底警官：“人们不怀疑我。这只是有着娃娃脸的塞思。我有分裂人格。我可以隐藏我所做的事情。他们抓不到我的把柄。这都是些间接的东西。”然而，随着卧底行动的进展，塞思并没有坦白，他告诉卧底警官他没有参与谋杀，并坚称是受雇于他父亲竞争对手之一的职业杀手对这起犯罪负责的故事。

52
01:03:08.000 --> 01:04:11.000
Seth's personal computer had been confiscated from the crime scene and an examination of its contents revealed a disturbing internet history. In the months leading up to the triple murder, searches were made online for poisons that could be easily disguised within food. An online purchase was made for the seeds of two types of highly lethal plants from a United States supplier, delivery expected in early July. The website of an Australian based seed supplier had also been visited, but their orders were temporarily unavailable. An email had been sent from Seth's computer to this supplier, requesting they make an exception, explaining it was his mother's 60th birthday the following weekend and he wanted to buy the seeds as a present. The email read, She has been looking for those particular seeds ever since she saw them in Florida last year. This email was misleading on two accounts.
塞思的个人电脑从犯罪现场被没收，对其内容的检查揭示了一段令人不安的互联网历史。在三起谋杀案发生前的几个月里，网上曾搜索过可以轻松伪装在食物中的毒药。有人从一家美国供应商那里在线购买了两种剧毒植物的种子，预计在7月初交货。一家澳大利亚本地种子供应商的网站也曾被访问过，但他们的订单暂时缺货。塞思的电脑曾向这家供应商发送了一电子邮件，要求他们通融一下，解释说下周末是他母亲的60岁生日，他想买这些种子作为礼物。邮件写道：“自从她去年在佛罗里达看到这些种子以来，她一直在寻找那些特定的种子。”这封电子邮件在两个方面具有误导性。

53
01:04:11.000 --> 01:05:29.000
Lover Gonzalez was only 43 years old, not 60, and she had not recently travelled to Florida. Seth denied performing the searches, ordering the seeds or sending the email, pinning the actions on his deceased father, claiming Teddy must have been researching the seeds online to ensure he didn't plan anything poisonous in the garden. Unbeknownst to Seth, police had found a vial of clear liquid taped under his desk during an earlier search of his bedroom. Scientific testing revealed the mysterious liquid to be a poisonous substance derived from one of the plants searched for online, highly lethal to anyone who consumed it. Days before her murder, Lover Gonzalez had been admitted to hospital after suffering from intense fever and severe abdominal pains. She suspected the culprit was undercooked food she consumed whilst dining out with her family, as Seth had also complained of feeling unwell after the meal. As such, she was diagnosed with colitis, an inflammation of the bowel associated with food poisoning. Lover received treatment and was discharged from hospital after an overnight stay.
洛伊弗·冈萨雷斯当时只有43岁，而不是60岁，而且她最近也没有去过佛罗里达。塞思否认自己曾进行过搜索、订购种子或发送电子邮件，并将这些行为归咎于他已故的父亲，声称泰迪一定是在网上研究种子，以确保他没有在花园里种植任何有毒的东西。塞思并不知道，警方在早期对他的卧室进行搜查时，在他的书桌下发现了一瓶用胶带固定住的透明液体。科学检测表明，这种神秘液体是从网上搜索过的植物中提取的有毒物质，对任何食用它的人来说都是剧毒。在她被谋杀几天前，洛伊弗·冈萨雷斯因遭受高烧和剧烈腹痛而被送往医院。她怀疑罪魁祸首是她与家人外出用餐时食用的未煮熟的食物，因为塞思也抱怨说饭后感觉不舒服。因此，她被诊断患有结肠炎，这是一种与食物中毒相关的肠道炎症。洛伊弗接受了治疗，并在住院一夜后出院。

54
01:05:29.000 --> 01:06:50.000
The link between the purchase of the poisonous seeds and Lover's sudden illness was not lost on investigators, who were coming to realise that the deaths of the Gonzalez family may have been months in the planning. The poisons weren't the only troublesome discovery within the internet history of Seth's computer. Frequent visits were also made to the webpage operated by Seth's number one fan, teenager Daisy Diaz, where she boasted about her love for the singer and raved about his outstanding personality, good looks and incredible talents. When investigators questioned Seth about his relationship with Daisy, he revealed she had recently passed away during the September 11 terrorist attacks on the World Trade Center. Seth claimed he had flown to New York City with Daisy's mother to attend the funeral. But investigators soon learned the truth. Daisy Diaz didn't exist. Her dedication page to Sethie and all its gushing posts of adoration was created and managed by Seth himself. In September 2001, Seth's relatives were left shaken and distraught when he broke the devastating news that he had been diagnosed with a brain tumour.
购买有毒种子与洛伊弗突然生病之间的联系并没有逃过调查人员的眼睛，他们开始意识到冈萨雷斯一家的死可能在几个月前就已经在策划了。毒药并不是塞思电脑互联网历史中唯一令人不安的发现。人们还频繁访问由塞思的头号粉丝、十几岁的黛西·迪亚兹（Daisy Diaz）运营的网页，她在网页上吹嘘自己对这位歌手的爱，并对他出色的个性、长相和不可思议的才华赞不绝口。当调查人员就他与黛西的关系盘问塞思时，他透露她在9·11世界贸易中心恐怖袭击事件中最近不幸遇难。塞思声称自己和黛西的母亲一起飞往纽约市参加葬礼。但调查人员很快得知了真相。黛西·迪亚兹根本不存在。她为塞思设立的奉献页面以及所有那些充满崇拜的帖子都是塞思自己创建和管理的。2001年9月，塞思的亲戚们在他爆出自己被诊断出患有脑瘤的毁灭性消息时，感到震惊和心烦意乱。

55
01:06:50.000 --> 01:08:09.000
He contacted his aunt Annie to inform her of the grim diagnosis, requesting she sent him $190,000 to pay for life-saving surgery. Annie, who was responsible for managing Teddy's overseas investment properties, was immediately suspicious of her nephew's claims. She refused his monetary request, instead informing the police about her concerns. By this stage, Seth had not yet gained access to his deceased family's multi-million dollar estate and his request for further victim compensation payments had been refused by the government. Seth did manage to amass approximately $88,000 by selling his parents' cars, his mother's jewellery, and his beloved Ford Festiva. In the following month of October, Seth placed the deposit on a $175,000 Lexus SC 430, telling the car dealership he would pay the remaining balance when his inheritance money came through. Seth eventually had to cancel the order for the Lexus as he was unable to come up with the remaining balance. He purchased the more affordable car instead, personalizing the license plate to read TLCS, the initials of the first names of his immediate family.
他联系了他的阿姨安妮，将严峻的诊断结果通知她，并请求她寄给他19万澳元来支付挽救生命的的手术费用。负责管理泰迪海外投资房产的安妮立即对她侄子的说法产生怀疑。她拒绝了他的金钱请求，转而将她的担忧告知了警方。在这个阶段，塞思还没有获得他已故家人的数百万美元遗产，政府也拒绝了他对进一步受害者赔偿金的请求。塞思确实通过出售父母的汽车、母亲的珠宝以及他心爱的福特福斯蒂瓦，聚敛了大约8.8万澳元。在接下来的10月，塞思为一辆价值17.5万澳元的雷克萨斯SC 430支付了定金，并告诉汽车经销商，等他的遗产资金到账时，他会支付剩余的尾款。塞思最终不得不取消雷克萨斯的订单，因为他拿不出剩余的尾款。相反，他购买了一辆更实惠的汽车，并将车牌个性化定制为“TLCS”，即他直系亲属名字的首字母缩写。

56
01:08:09.000 --> 01:09:13.000
Since the murders, Seth moved between relatives' homes before he finally settled into a rental apartment on the 11th floor of a secured building in the North Shore suburb of Chatswood. The apartment's rent and bills were financed by his relatives, and Seth furnished it with property taken from his family's Collins Street home. He told relatives police recommended the relocation as a safety proportion, which was entirely untrue. In December, Seth's aunt, Emily Luna, agreed to attend the Gonzales residence to re-enact her version of events from the evening of July 10. Emily had arrived to the house at 6pm, with the impression someone was home. She spotted Seth's Ford Festiva in the carport and noticed it was empty. She had seen what she believed was a figure wearing a baseball cap and coat on the other side of the front door, standing in the foyer. But her young son had convinced her it was just a coat stand.
谋杀案发生后，塞思在亲戚的家之间辗转，直到最后安顿在北岸查茨伍德郊区一栋戒备森严的大楼11楼的一套出租公寓里。这套公寓的租金和账单由他的亲戚资助，塞思用从他家人柯林斯街家中拿走的财产布置了它。他告诉亲戚，警察建议将搬迁作为安全预防措施，这完全是谎言。12月，塞思的姑姑艾米丽·卢娜同意前往冈萨雷斯住宅，重新演绎她对7月10日晚事情经过的看法。艾米丽于下午6点到达房子，带着家里有人的印象。她在车棚里看到了塞思的福特福斯蒂瓦，并注意到它是空的。她看到她认为是穿着棒球帽和外套的身影站在前门另一侧的门厅里。但她的小儿子说服她那只是一个衣帽架。

57
01:09:13.000 --> 01:10:44.000
During the December re-enactment, Emily realized the coat stand in the foyer was actually situated much further back from the front door than she originally thought. Emily was now certain it was a person she saw on the other side of the door that night, five foot, four inches tall, the same height as Seth Gonzales. By January 2002, Seth was made aware that investigators were doubting his alibi for the night of the murders. The Daily Telegraph newspaper reported that police were now following a line of inquiry around a green hatchback, similar to Seth's Ford Festiva. The undercover officer, still posing as Seth's gangster friend, also intentionally leaked information to Seth that witnesses had cited his empty vehicle at the front of his house on the afternoon of the murders. Seth was oblivious to the fact his phones were bugged and his calls were being monitored and recorded by police. During a phone call to a friend dated January 10, Seth admitted his original alibi on the night of the murders had been a lie, but he had a new one that he was certain would convince police of his innocence, although he admitted he was worried it could, quote, blow up in his face again. After this call, police confronted Seth about his alibi and he decided to come clean.
在12月的案情重演期间，艾米丽意识到门厅里的衣帽架实际上比她最初想象的离前门要远得多. 艾米丽现在确信，那天晚上她在门另一侧看到的是一个人，身高五英尺四英寸，与赛斯·冈萨雷斯身高相同. 到2002年1月，赛斯开始意识到调查人员在怀疑他谋杀当晚的不在场证明. 《每日电讯报》报道称，警方目前正围绕一辆绿色两厢车展开调查，这与赛斯的福特Festiva相似. 这名仍在冒充赛斯黑帮朋友的便衣警察，还故意向赛斯透露信息，称有目击者在谋杀案发生当天下午看到他的空车停在房前. 赛斯并不知道他的电话被窃听，他的通话也一直受到警方的监控和录音. 在1月10日打给朋友的一通电话中，赛斯承认他最初关于谋杀当晚的不在场证明是个谎言，但他有了一个新证明，他确信这能让警方相信他是无辜的，尽管他承认自己担心这可能会“再次搞砸”. 在这通电话后，警方就他的不在场证明与赛斯进行了对质，他决定坦白.

58
01:10:44.000 --> 01:11:46.000
Seth did not go driving around Kingsgrove looking for his friend's new house on the night of the murders. He had actually visited a sex worker. He wasn't upfront about it initially as he was concerned the act could bring shame upon his religious family, who believed he was a virgin. Seth now claimed that on the evening of the murders, he left his father's legal office just before 4pm. He parked his car at home before walking to a nearby petrol station where he caught a taxi to a brothel located in Chatswood. He left his car at home because he didn't want to risk someone citing it near the brothel. Seth engaged in the services of a sex worker and boasted she tried to refuse his payment because the sex was so good. Afterwards, Seth walked to Chatswood train station where he caught a taxi back home to Collins Street. He got straight into his car and drove to his friend Sam's place for their scheduled 8pm meetup.
谋杀当晚，赛斯并没有开车在金斯格罗夫寻找他朋友的新房子. 他实际上是去找了一名性工作者. 起初他没有直说，是因为担心这种行为会给他的宗教家庭带来耻辱，因为他的家人一直认为他是处男. 赛斯现在声称，在谋杀案当晚，他在下午4点前不久离开了父亲的律师事务所. 他把车停在家裡，然后步行到一个附近的加油站，在那里坐出租车去了一家位于查茨伍德的妓院. 他把车留在家里，是因为他不想冒着被人看到车停在妓院附近的风险. 赛斯接受了一名性工作者的服务，并吹嘘说对方甚至想免收他的服务费，因为他表现太好了. 此后，赛斯步行到查茨伍德火车站，坐出租车回到了科林斯街的家中. 他直接上车，开车去了朋友萨姆的家，参加他们原定晚上8点举行的聚会.

59
01:11:46.000 --> 01:12:59.000
As they continued to monitor Seth's phone calls, police were aware that Seth had recently been contacting numerous brothels in the North Shore area. Around the same time, they noticed he was having telecommunications with an unknown male. Officers tracked down this man and paid him a visit to inquire about his relationship with Seth and the purpose of their recent phone calls. The man was a local taxi driver. He revealed Seth had approached him at the taxi rank at Chatswood train station on January 12, 2002, 5 months after the triple murder. Seth offered the taxi driver $50 to write a formal statement confirming that he had picked Seth up on the evening of July 10, 2001 and had dropped him off at a brothel. Seth reassured the taxi driver the request didn't relate to anything serious. When police informed the driver that Seth was implicated in a triple homicide, he immediately retracted his statement, which was just as well as his driving records for the evening of July 10 failed to support Seth's new alibi.
随着警方继续监听赛斯的电话，他们发现赛斯最近一直在联系北岸地区的许多妓院. 大约在同一时间，他们注意到他与一名身份不明的男性有通讯往来. 警官们找到了这名男子，并登门拜访，询问他与赛斯的关系以及他们最近频繁通话的目的. 这名男子是一名当地的出租车司机. 他透露，在2002年1月12日，即三起谋杀案发生5个月后，赛斯曾在查茨伍德火车站的出租车排队处接近他. 赛斯给这名出租车司机50美元，让他写一份正式声明，证实他在2001年7月10日晚上接了赛斯，并把他送到了一家妓院. 赛斯向出租车司机保证，这个要求不涉及任何严重的事情. 当警方告知司机赛斯卷入了一起三亚谋杀案时，他立即撤回了自己的声明，这也正好印证了他在7月10日晚上的驾驶记录无法支持赛斯的新不在场证明.

60
01:12:59.000 --> 01:14:11.000
